{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004087-creepypastas-in-wod","id":1004087,"title":"Creepypastas in WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-16T13:25:51-08:00","id":1004087,"title":"Creepypastas in WoD","content":"Has anyone adopted a Creepypasta story in their WoD games?<br /> <br /> Well let's start with Candle Cove for example<br /> <br /> Well for one thing there's already a real play of a mortal's game of <a href=\"http://actualplay.roleplayingpublicradio.com/2010/03/genre/horror/world-of-darkness-candle-cove/\" target=\"_blank\">Candle Cove</a> which is Chronicles of Darkness however which painted the Skin-Taker as a demon abducting children in it's own realm if I'm positive.<br /> <br /> Well there's also the recent <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Series/ChannelZero\" target=\"_blank\">Channel Zero</a> which has recently completed it's first season with it's finale called &quot;Welcome Home&quot; which revealed infact that Candle Cove infact a creation of the protagonists long dead twin brother Eddie who aims to possess his other brother Mike's body. If anyone here has watched the Channel Zero episodes, I wonder what supernatural what Eddie would be? Is he a Marauder Mage which Candle Cove is his personal horizon realm?<br /> <br /> Lastly Candle Cove's <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/WMG/CandleCove\" target=\"_blank\">WMG page</a> lists some possibilities on what Candle Cove might actually be which could be used for anyone's personal discretion although I personally choose this one probably being the creepiest one due to the fact I'm more in the angle of Candle Cove being a bizarre puppet world of it's own :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Candle Cove was real...<br /> ...But not as a show. The girl who was Janice was really in a place/world where the only other inhabitants were puppets or puppet like things. She was forced to go &quot;adventuring&quot; with them. And they were all somehow constantly being recorded. What was seen by others wasn't filmed with a camera, it was through something else's eyes. This could explain why Janice was said to sometimes breakdown crying... </div> </div> </div>Lastly, I wonder how to have supernatural PCs like Kindred, Garou, Mages, etc to encounter these particular adoptions of Creepypastas? For example, what about having a Kindred character who has a troubling or nightmarish past when they were mortal for example she used to live in a town called <a href=\"http://ichor-falls.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Ichor Falls</a> when she was a child before moving to the city or has a relative there. As she grew up there, she probably watched Candle Cove back in 1971/1972 and still has nightmares from it among other disturbing things surrounding that town even after post-embrace till she get's fed up with it decides to travel to her old childhood town to get to the bottom of this and maybe her coterie comes to accompany her.<br /> <br /> Although I think this scenario would probably work best in Requiem than Masquerade but maybe it doesn't matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-16-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}